{
  "translations": [
    {
      "verseSection": "verse-1",
      "english": "Now the serpent was cunning, more than any beast of the field that Awtsmoos Elokim had made. And it said to the woman, \"Indeed, has Elokim said, 'You shall not eat from any tree of the garden'?\""
    },
    {
      "verseSection": "verse-2",
      "english": "And the woman said to the serpent, \"From the fruit of the trees of the garden we may eat."
    },
    {
      "verseSection": "verse-3",
      "english": "But from the fruit of the tree that is in the midst of the garden, Elokim said, 'You shall not eat from it, and you shall not touch it, lest you die.'\""
    },
    {
      "verseSection": "verse-4",
      "english": "And the serpent said to the woman, \"You shall surely not die."
    },
    {
      "verseSection": "verse-5",
      "english": "For Elokim knows that on the day you eat from it, your eyes will be opened, and you will be like Elokim, knowing good and evil.\""
    },
    {
      "verseSection": "verse-6",
      "english": "And the woman saw that the tree was good for food, and that it was a delight to the eyes, and that the tree was desirable to make one wise. So she took from its fruit and ate, and she also gave to her husband who was with her, and he ate."
    }
  ]
}
